    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [102/60, 102/61, 102/62, 102/63, 102/09, 102/70A, 102/72A, 102/73A, 102/75A, 102/76, 102/77; Received: 05/03/2026. 102/66, 102/65; Received: 16/03/2026. 102/71B; Received: 09/06/2026].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - No additional windows or openings shall be formed in the side elevation of the development hereby permitted.\r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' privacy.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - The roof of the existing single-storey rear extension shall not be used as a balcony, roof terrace, roof garden, sitting-out area, or for any other form of external amenity space at any time. No furniture, privacy screens, balustrades, decking, or other paraphernalia associated with such use shall be placed on the roof. \r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' privacy \r\n\r\n"
